- Fixed fleetd silently removing the BitLocker startup PIN requirement from a Windows host when it rotated the host's recovery key. Rotation added a TPM-only protector even when the volume already had a TPM and PIN protector, and the added protector unlocked the volume at startup without the PIN. fleetd now adds a TPM protector only when the volume has no protector that can already unlock it at startup.
- Fixed fleetd ignoring a paused BitLocker encryption or decryption on a Windows host. fleetd now resumes a paused encryption, and reports a paused decryption to Fleet so the reason appears in the host's disk encryption details.
